cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "When does a black hole stop being a one-way door? Certified Page evaporation constants for a Schwarzschild black hole emitting photons and gravitons"
authors:
  - name: "Moki & Julio"
version: "1.0"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - Hawking radiation
  - Page time
  - black hole entropy
  - greybody factors
  - Schwarzschild black hole
  - Regge-Wheeler equation
  - computer-assisted proof
  - interval arithmetic
  - ball arithmetic
  - rigorous numerics
abstract: >-
  To our knowledge, the first certified (interval-arithmetic, rigorously error-bounded) enclosures of Page's
  evaporation constants for a Schwarzschild black hole emitting photons and gravitons into empty space: beta =
  1.4846916919 +- 7.81e-11 and Page time t*/t_decay = 0.5381024532 +- 8.99e-11, together with certified photon power,
  total power alpha and photon and graviton entropy rates (search of arXiv, INSPIRE and Zenodo to 17 November 2026).
  The graviton power, and so the graviton part of alpha, was
  certified earlier by Newton (Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.22800587) to 1% width; our independent
  enclosure lies inside his interval and is about seven orders of magnitude narrower. The result settles the digits
  Page (2013) flagged as uncertain. Sealed test (one earlier sealed failure listed), two internal referee rounds,
  blind replication by an independent, non-rigorous formulation (Teukolsky + MST series).
